                <pb facs="0522" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/139: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-22T12:00:00-05:00">April 22, 1939—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Your 108, March 29, 5 p.m. Please inform the Italian authorities that Mr.
                    Duncan Henry at Addis Ababa is now authorized to represent the Presbyterian
                    Board of Foreign Missions in negotiations relating to the appraisal of mission
                    properties at Sayo and Gore.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
